   137→    features:
   138→      - _ulid: 01KJP2768T96S8870BH36ZE76K
   139→        slugs:
   140→          - daemon-agent-dispatch
   141→        title: Daemon Agent Dispatch Integration
   142→        type: feature
   143→        tags: []
   144→        description: |
   145→          Agent dispatch API routes in the daemon, enhanced file watcher with
   146→          task state diffing for change detection, CLI event emission endpoint,
   147→          and WebSocket broadcasts for agent invocation status.
   148→        acceptance_criteria:
   149→          - id: ac-1
   150→            given: |
   151→              The daemon is running with dispatch enabled
   152→            when: |
   153→              The file watcher detects a change in project.tasks.yaml
   154→            then: |
   155→              The watcher parses the new task states, diffs against the
   156→              previously cached states, and emits state change events to
   157→              the dispatch engine for each detected transition
   158→          - id: ac-2
   159→            given: |
   160→              A CLI command changes task state (e.g. kspec task start)
   161→            when: |
   162→              The daemon is running
   163→            then: |
   164→              The CLI posts a JSON event to POST /api/agent/events containing
   165→              task_id, previous_status, new_status, and timestamp
   166→          - id: ac-3
   167→            given: |
   168→              The daemon receives a state change event matching dispatch rules
   169→            when: |
   170→              The dispatch engine processes it
   171→            then: |
   172→              The agent is dispatched and a status event is broadcast on the
   173→              agents WebSocket topic
   174→          - id: ac-4
   175→            given: |
   176→              A WebSocket client subscribes to agent status updates
   177→            when: |
   178→              An agent invocation starts, completes, or fails
   179→            then: |
   180→              A broadcast event is sent containing session_id, agent_id,
   181→              task_id, status, and timestamp
   182→          - id: ac-5
   183→            given: |
   184→              GET /api/agent/status is called
   185→            when: |
   186→              The dispatch engine is running
   187→            then: |
   188→              Returns JSON with active invocations array, queue depth number,
   189→              dispatch_enabled boolean, and agent_definitions array
   190→          - id: ac-6
   191→            given: |
   192→              POST /api/agent/dispatch is called with action start or stop
   193→            when: |
   194→              The request is from localhost
   195→            then: |
   196→              The dispatch engine starts or stops and returns JSON with the
   197→              new dispatch_enabled state
   198→          - id: ac-7
   199→            given: |
   200→              The daemon is not running
   201→            when: |
   202→              A CLI command changes task state
   203→            then: |
   204→              The event emission POST fails silently with no error to the
   205→              user — dispatch requires a running daemon
   206→          - id: ac-8
   207→            given: The dispatch engine runs an agent invocation
   208→            when: The agent produces text output (agent_message_chunk events)
   209→            then: The daemon broadcasts each text chunk on the agents WebSocket topic with type
   210→              agent_text_chunk, session_id, agent_id, task_id, text, and timestamp
