   264→          - ws-disconnect-lifecycle-cleanup
   265→        title: WebSocket Disconnect Lifecycle Cleanup
   266→        type: requirement
   267→        tags:
   268→          - daemon
   269→          - websocket
   270→          - reliability
   271→        description: Ensure daemon WebSocket disconnect handling is accurate for abnormal closes. Disconnect
   272→          events must reliably identify the same session created on connect, remove that session
   273→          from in-memory registries, and prevent stale heartbeat/client counts after client
   274→          disconnect or process termination.
   275→        depends_on: []
   276→        implements: []
   277→        relates_to: []
   278→        tests: []
   279→        traits: []
   280→        notes: []
   281→        created: 2026-03-03T22:03:28.854Z
   282→        acceptance_criteria:
   283→          - id: ac-1
   284→            given: multiple clients are connected and one disconnects
   285→            when: GET /api/health is requested
   286→            then: the connections field reflects only currently active sessions
   287→          - id: ac-3
   288→            given: a disconnected session was previously in heartbeat monitoring
   289→            when: the next heartbeat interval executes
   290→            then: the daemon does not attempt to ping that session and emits no stale heartbeat ping log for it
   291→          - id: ac-2
   292→            given: a WebSocket client disconnects unexpectedly with close code 1006
   293→            when: the daemon close handler runs
   294→            then: the session is removed from pubsub connection tracking and the disconnect log includes that
   295→              session id rather than undefined
