   462→    slugs:
   463→      - web-dashboard
   464→    title: Web Dashboard
   465→    type: feature
   466→    tags:
   467→      - svelte
   468→      - ui
   469→      - dashboard
   470→    description: |
   471→      SvelteKit-based web interface for viewing and editing specs, tasks, inbox, and session state.
   472→      Uses shadcn-svelte components for accessible UI. Connects to daemon via REST API and WebSocket
   473→      for real-time updates. Includes WebSocketManager for connection resilience with exponential
   474→      backoff reconnection and sequence deduplication.
   475→    depends_on:
   476→      - "@api-contract"
   477→    implements: []
   478→    relates_to: []
   479→    tests: []
   480→    traits:
   481→      - "@trait-filterable-list"
   482→      - "@trait-websocket-protocol"
   483→    notes: []
   484→    created: 2026-01-22T01:18:11.366Z
   485→    acceptance_criteria:
   486→      - id: ac-1
   487→        given: daemon is running on configured port (default 3456)
   488→        when: browser opens the daemon URL
   489→        then: dashboard shows task overview with ready, in_progress, pending_review, blocked, completed
   490→          counts
   491→      - id: ac-2
   492→        given: dashboard is displayed
   493→        when: task counts update on server
   494→        then: counts animate to new values without page refresh (WebSocket-driven)
   495→      - id: ac-3
   496→        given: dashboard is displayed
   497→        when: user clicks a task count badge
   498→        then: navigates to task list filtered by that status
   499→      - id: ac-4
   500→        given: user is viewing task list
   501→        when: list loads
   502→        then: shows task title, status badge, priority indicator, spec_ref link, notes count
   503→      - id: ac-5
   504→        given: user is viewing task list
   505→        when: clicking a task row
   506→        then: task detail panel opens showing description, notes (chronological), todos, dependencies
   507→      - id: ac-6
   508→        given: user is viewing task detail
   509→        when: task has spec_ref
   510→        then: spec reference is clickable link to spec item detail
   511→      - id: ac-7
   512→        given: user is viewing task detail
   513→        when: user clicks Start Task button
   514→        then: POST to /api/tasks/:ref/start, task status updates, UI reflects change
   515→      - id: ac-8
   516→        given: user is viewing task detail
   517→        when: user types in note textarea and clicks Add Note
   518→        then: POST to /api/tasks/:ref/note, note appears in list
   519→      - id: ac-9
   520→        given: user is viewing task list
   521→        when: filter controls are visible
   522→        then: can filter by status, type, tag, assignee, automation status
   523→      - id: ac-10
   524→        given: user applies filter
   525→        when: filter selection changes
   526→        then: URL updates with query params, list updates without full reload
   527→      - id: ac-11
   528→        given: user navigates to /items
   529→        when: spec tree displays
   530→        then: shows hierarchical tree with modules > features > requirements, expand/collapse
   531→      - id: ac-12
   532→        given: user clicks spec item in tree
   533→        when: item detail panel opens
   534→        then: shows title, description, acceptance criteria (GWT format), traits, implementation status
   535→      - id: ac-13
   536→        given: spec item has linked tasks
   537→        when: viewing item detail
   538→        then: Implementation section shows linked tasks with their status
   539→      - id: ac-14
   540→        given: spec item has traits
   541→        when: viewing item detail
   542→        then: Traits section shows trait titles as chips, clickable to trait detail
   543→      - id: ac-15
